Upstream: 86b23609d5e1 ("clk: qcom: gdsc: tear down genpds in unregister")
Subject: clk: qcom: gdsc: tear down genpds in unregister

gdsc_register() calls pm_genpd_init() for every GDSC, but gdsc_unregister()
never removed them, so a driver unbind/rebind always collided with the name
already in 'pm_genpd' ("debugfs: 'titan_top_gdsc' already exists"), after
which camcc-sc8280xp failed to probe with -E22. On gaokun3 that left the
camera subsystem unbound and unbindable until a reboot; the failure was
captured in pstore. The upstream fix also swaps the order, removing the OF
provider before tearing its subdomains down.

Adapted from the gaokun-android port, where the pstore log was recorded.
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
@@ -678,10 +678,18 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 void gdsc_unregister(struct gdsc_desc *desc)
 {
 	struct device *dev = desc->dev;
+	struct gdsc **scs = desc->scs;
 	size_t num = desc->num;
+	int i;
 
-	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, num);
 	of_genpd_del_provider(dev->of_node);
+	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, num);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < num; i++) {
+		if (!scs[i])
+			continue;
+		pm_genpd_remove(&scs[i]->pd);
+	}
 }
 
